# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored and must stay that way.

# Supabase: use the TRANSACTION POOLER string (port 6543), not the direct
# connection. Direct connections run out of slots under serverless, and the
# session pooler does not free them between invocations.
#
#   Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> Database -> Connection string
#   -> "Transaction pooler"  (host ends in .pooler.supabase.com, port 6543)
#
# The driver sets sslmode=require when the URL does not say otherwise: encrypted,
# but the server certificate is not verified. Append ?sslmode=verify-full once
# the provider CA is configured.
# Uncomment and fill in. Leaving it commented keeps the filesystem store.
# CURB_POSTGRES_URL=postgres://postgres.PROJECTREF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# Optional. Defaults to public.
# CURB_POSTGRES_SCHEMA=public

# Set to 1 if your network's resolver hijacks DNS for the chain RPC hostname
# (symptom: every chain agent reports SOURCE_UNREACHABLE and the TLS error names
# a certificate for some other domain). Resolves over HTTPS to Cloudflare while
# TLS still validates against the real hostname. Not needed on a platform with
# an honest resolver.
# CURB_DNS_OVER_HTTPS=1

# Protects POST /api/tick. Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# The same value goes into the scheduler (GitHub Actions secret CURB_TICK_SECRET).
# Leave unset locally and /api/tick accepts unauthenticated GETs for development.
# CURB_TICK_SECRET=

# Optional. Narrates yesterday's Gazette lede with Claude, once per closed day.
# The prose passes the same policy gate as every agent; the model may repeat
# the record's figures verbatim and may not add one. Without a key the
# templated lede stands and the page says a narration was not configured.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. A Discord or Slack incoming-webhook URL. After every tick the
# conditions a person should know about — an absent agent, a paused feed, the
# stock-token beacon pointing somewhere new — are compared with the last set
# delivered, and what changed is posted once. Unconfigured is reported in the
# tick response as NOT_CONFIGURED; nothing is assumed to have paged anyone.
# CURB_ALERT_WEBHOOK=
